## ABSTRACT

This paper presents a formal re-examination of Erwin Schrödinger's 1918 transposition of the cosmological constant from the left-hand side to the right-hand side of Einstein's field equations. We argue that this algebraic exercise constituted the first logical deduction of a repulsive, anti-gravity force from the foundations of general relativity.

Critically, we expose a foundational error in modern cosmology: the predictive successes attributed to the dark matter and dark energy paradigm are not products of accurate physical accounting, but rather the result of **misattributing observable gravitational anomalies to hypothetical, post-hoc entities**. We demonstrate that the same anomalies—galactic rotation curves, cosmic acceleration, and large-scale void dynamics—are structurally predicted *a priori* by the geometric inversion inherent in Schrödinger's transposition, requiring no free parameters or unobserved particles.

Einstein dismissed Schrödinger's interpretation as opening a "Pandora's Box." We argue that this box, once opened, reveals that the dark matter and dark energy paradigm is a product of broken models and circular reasoning—not of physical reality. The anti-gravity paradigm, grounded in the exact algebraic symmetry of general relativity, resolves the cosmological crisis without invoking a single hypothetical entity.

